<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>SparqOS relationships</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Host+Grotesk:wght@300;400;500&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style is:inline>
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
:root {
  --bg: #1A1A1A;
  --bg2: #222222;
  --bg3: #2a2a2a;
  --text: #E5E5E5;
  --text2: rgba(229,229,229,0.6);
  --text3: rgba(229,229,229,0.35);
  --border: rgba(229,229,229,0.08);
  --border2: rgba(229,229,229,0.14);
  --green: #35B98F;
  --green-dim: rgba(53,185,143,0.08);
  --green-border: rgba(53,185,143,0.3);
  --purple: #B0AAEE;
  --purple-dim: rgba(127,119,221,0.08);
  --purple-border: rgba(127,119,221,0.3);
  --amber: #F4B84A;
  --amber-dim: rgba(239,159,39,0.08);
  --amber-border: rgba(239,159,39,0.28);
  --red: #E87070;
  --red-dim: rgba(226,75,74,0.08);
  --red-border: rgba(226,75,74,0.28);
  --domain: #7BB2D4;
  --domain-dim: rgba(123,178,212,0.08);
  --domain-border: rgba(123,178,212,0.3);
  --grey: #9A9A9A;
  --font: 'Host Grotesk', sans-serif;
  --mono: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
}
html, body {
  width: 100%; min-height: 100vh;
  background: var(--bg);
  color: var(--text);
  font-family: var(--font);
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}

/* ── HEADER ── */
header {
  padding: 36px 48px 24px;
  border-bottom: 0.5px solid var(--border);
  display: flex; align-items: flex-start; justify-content: space-between;
  flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 24px;
}
.header-left h1 {
  font-size: 28px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  margin-bottom: 8px;
}
.header-left p {
  font-size: 14px; color: var(--text2); max-width: 620px; line-height: 1.6;
}
.header-right {
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-end; gap: 12px;
}
.legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; justify-content: flex-end; }
.legend-item {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .06em;
  text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text3);
}
.legend-dot { width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; flex-shrink: 0; }
.control-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; align-items: center; justify-content: flex-end; }
.control-label {
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: .06em;
  text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text3);
}
.pill {
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .05em;
  padding: 5px 12px;
  border-radius: 100px; border: 0.5px solid var(--border2);
  background: none; color: var(--text3); cursor: pointer;
  transition: all .2s;
}
.pill:hover { color: var(--text); border-color: var(--border2); }
.pill.lens { border-color: var(--purple-border); }
.pill.lens:hover { color: var(--purple); }
.pill.lens.active { background: var(--purple-dim); border-color: var(--purple-border); color: var(--purple); }
.pill.view.active { background: rgba(229,229,229,0.08); border-color: var(--border2); color: var(--text); }

/* ── MAIN LAYOUT ── */
main {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 360px;
  min-height: calc(100vh - 190px);
}

/* ── DIAGRAM ── */
.diagram { padding: 28px 32px 40px; overflow: auto; }
main.view-list .diagram { display: none; }
main:not(.view-list) .list-wrap { display: none; }

.canvas {
  position: relative;
  width: 990px; height: 900px;
  margin: 0 auto;
}
#edges {
  position: absolute; inset: 0;
  width: 100%; height: 100%;
  z-index: 0; overflow: visible;
}
.band-label {
  position: absolute; z-index: 0;
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: .1em;
  text-transform: uppercase; color: rgba(229,229,229,0.18);
  white-space: nowrap; pointer-events: none;
}

/* ── EDGES ── */
.edge-line { fill: none; stroke: rgba(229,229,229,0.22); stroke-width: 1; transition: stroke .2s, stroke-width .2s; }
.edge-hit { fill: none; stroke: transparent; stroke-width: 14px; cursor: help; }
.edge { transition: opacity .25s; }
.edge.dim { opacity: 0.06; }
.edge.active .edge-line { stroke-width: 1.6; }
.edge:hover .edge-line { stroke: var(--text) !important; stroke-width: 1.8; }

/* ── NODES ── */
.node {
  position: absolute; z-index: 1;
  width: 170px;
  border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px 12px;
  border: 0.5px solid var(--border2);
  background: var(--bg2);
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: opacity .25s, transform .2s, box-shadow .2s;
}
.node:hover { transform: translateY(-1px); box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); }
.node:focus-visible { outline: 1.5px solid var(--text); outline-offset: 2px; }
.node-name {
  font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.3;
  margin-bottom: 3px; color: var(--text);
}
.node-sub {
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: .03em;
  color: var(--text3); line-height: 1.4;
}
.node.dim { opacity: 0.12; }
.node.dim:hover { opacity: 0.25; transform: none; box-shadow: none; }

.open-flag {
  display: inline-block; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 8px;
  letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase;
  padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 3px; margin-top: 6px;
  background: rgba(239,159,39,0.16); color: var(--amber);
  border: 0.5px solid var(--amber-border);
}

.node-found { background: var(--amber-dim); border-color: var(--amber-border); }
.node-found .node-name { color: var(--amber); }
.node-delivery { background: var(--purple-dim); border-color: var(--purple-border); }
.node-delivery .node-name { color: var(--purple); }
.node-store { background: var(--domain-dim); border-color: var(--domain-border); }
.node-store .node-name { color: var(--domain); }
.node-surface { background: var(--green-dim); border-color: var(--green-border); }
.node-surface .node-name { color: var(--green); }
.node-gtm { background: var(--red-dim); border-color: var(--red-border); }
.node-gtm .node-name { color: var(--red); }
.node-external { background: rgba(229,229,229,0.02); border-color: var(--border); border-style: dashed; }
.node-external .node-name { color: var(--text2); }
.node-engagement { background: rgba(229,229,229,0.06); border-color: rgba(229,229,229,0.4); }
.node-engagement .node-name { color: var(--text); }

/* ── DEPTH MARKER ── */
.depth-mark {
  position: absolute; right: 9px; bottom: 7px;
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; line-height: 1;
  color: var(--text3); transition: color .2s, transform .2s;
}
.node.drilled .depth-mark { color: var(--text); transform: rotate(180deg); }
.depth-key {
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--text3);
  width: 8px; display: inline-block; text-align: center;
}

/* ── SIDEBAR ── */
.sidebar {
  border-left: 0.5px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--bg2);
  overflow-y: auto;
}
.sidebar-section { padding: 20px 24px; border-bottom: 0.5px solid var(--border); }
.sidebar-title {
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: .08em;
  text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text3); margin-bottom: 12px;
}
.detail-empty { font-size: 12px; color: var(--text3); line-height: 1.6; font-style: italic; }
#node-detail { display: none; }
#node-detail.visible { display: block; }
.detail-name { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 6px; line-height: 1.35; }
.detail-kind {
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: .07em;
  text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text3); margin-bottom: 10px;
}
.detail-desc { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text2); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 14px; }
.detail-bullets { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 14px; }
.detail-bullets li {
  font-size: 12px; color: var(--text2); line-height: 1.6;
  padding-left: 12px; position: relative; margin-bottom: 10px;
  padding-bottom: 10px; border-bottom: 0.5px solid var(--border);
}
.detail-bullets li:last-child { border-bottom: none; margin-bottom: 0; padding-bottom: 0; }
.detail-bullets li::before { content: '·'; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--text3); }
.detail-meta { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
.meta-row { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 5px; }
.meta-label {
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: .07em;
  text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text3);
}
.meta-value { font-size: 12px; color: var(--text2); line-height: 1.5; }
.meta-value a { text-decoration: none; }
.meta-value a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
.chip-list { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px; }
.chip {
  display: inline-block; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 500;
  padding: 2px 8px; line-height: 1.5;
  border-radius: 10px; border: 0.5px solid var(--border2);
  background: var(--bg); color: var(--text2);
  cursor: pointer; transition: opacity .2s;
}
.chip:hover { opacity: 0.75; }
.chip-found { background: var(--amber-dim); border-color: var(--amber-border); color: var(--amber); }
.chip-delivery { background: var(--purple-dim); border-color: var(--purple-border); color: var(--purple); }
.chip-store { background: var(--domain-dim); border-color: var(--domain-border); color: var(--domain); }
.chip-surface { background: var(--green-dim); border-color: var(--green-border); color: var(--green); }
.chip-gtm { background: var(--red-dim); border-color: var(--red-border); color: var(--red); }
.chip-external { background: rgba(229,229,229,0.02); border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text3); }
.chip-engagement { background: rgba(229,229,229,0.06); border-color: rgba(229,229,229,0.4); color: var(--text); }

/* ── DRILL-IN ── */
.drill-back {
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: .06em;
  text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text3);
  background: none; border: none; padding: 0; margin-bottom: 10px;
  cursor: pointer; transition: color .2s;
}
.drill-back:hover { color: var(--text); }
.drill-group { margin-bottom: 16px; }
.drill-group:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.drill-group-label {
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: .07em;
  text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text3);
  margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 5px;
  border-bottom: 0.5px solid var(--border);
}
.drill-item {
  font-size: 12px; color: var(--text2); line-height: 1.55;
  padding-left: 12px; position: relative; margin-bottom: 7px;
}
.drill-item::before { content: '·'; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--text3); }
.drill-source {
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: .04em;
  color: var(--text3); margin-top: 6px; display: block;
}
.drill-source a { color: var(--domain); text-decoration: none; }
.drill-source a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
.drill-none {
  padding: 12px; border-radius: 6px; margin-top: 4px;
  background: rgba(229,229,229,0.03); border: 0.5px dashed var(--border2);
}
.drill-none-label {
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: .07em;
  text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text3); margin-bottom: 6px;
}
.drill-none-text { font-size: 12px; color: var(--text2); line-height: 1.55; }

.def-row { margin-bottom: 12px; }
.def-row:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.def-term { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 3px; }
.def-body { font-size: 12px; color: var(--text2); line-height: 1.55; }

.open-card {
  padding: 10px 12px; border-radius: 6px;
  background: var(--amber-dim); border: 0.5px solid var(--amber-border);
  margin-bottom: 8px;
}
.open-card:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.open-card-label {
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: .08em;
  text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--amber); margin-bottom: 5px;
}
.open-card-text { font-size: 12px; color: var(--text2); line-height: 1.55; }

/* ── LIST VIEW ── */
.list-wrap { padding: 28px 40px 48px; max-width: 900px; }
.list-intro { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text2); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 24px; max-width: 620px; }
.list-group { margin-bottom: 26px; padding-bottom: 20px; border-bottom: 0.5px solid var(--border); }
.list-group:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
.list-group-name { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 3px; }
.list-group-sub {
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: .05em;
  text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text3); margin-bottom: 12px;
}
.rel { display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: baseline; padding: 4px 0; }
.rel-arrow {
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--text3);
  width: 22px; flex-shrink: 0;
}
.rel-arrow.bi { color: var(--purple); }
.rel-text { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text2); line-height: 1.5; }
.rel-none { font-size: 12px; color: var(--text3); font-style: italic; }

footer {
  padding: 18px 48px;
  border-top: 0.5px solid var(--border);
  display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px;
}
.footer-text {
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .05em;
  color: var(--text3); text-transform: uppercase;
}

@media (max-width: 1100px) {
  main { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .sidebar { border-left: none; border-top: 0.5px solid var(--border); }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header>
  <div class="header-left">
    <h1>SparqOS relationships</h1>
    <p>Not a hierarchy — a set of things that inform each other. Every line is a claim about direction: who feeds whom, and where the feed runs both ways. The engagement is what drives it; ADLC is the engine it moves through; the store is the memory underneath; GTM is what the two of them make sellable. Click a node to isolate what it touches, and again to drop one altitude inside it — where an interior has actually been defined.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="header-right">
    <div class="legend" id="legend"></div>
    <div class="control-row" id="view-select"></div>
    <div class="control-row" id="lens-select"></div>
  </div>
</header>

<main id="main">
  <div class="diagram">
    <div class="canvas" id="canvas">
      <svg id="edges"></svg>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="list-wrap">
    <div class="list-intro">Every relationship on the map, written out. <span style="color:var(--purple)">↔</span> marks a loop — both sides inform each other. This list and the map are generated from the same source, so they cannot drift apart.</div>
    <div id="list-body"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="sidebar">
    <div class="sidebar-section">
      <div class="sidebar-title">Selection</div>
      <div id="node-placeholder" class="detail-empty">Click any node — or any lens — to see what it informs, what informs it, and where the relationship runs both ways.</div>
      <div id="node-detail"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="sidebar-section">
      <div class="sidebar-title">The two stores</div>
      <div class="def-row">
        <div class="def-term">SPOT — the data lake</div>
        <div class="def-body">The store of what happened in Sparq history. The record, not the reading of it.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="def-row">
        <div class="def-term">Institutional intelligence</div>
        <div class="def-body">The store of what the data lake teaches. The reading, not the record.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="def-row">
        <div class="def-term">Context flow / retrieval</div>
        <div class="def-body">Neither store — the layer that gets what is stored in front of the work.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="def-row">
        <div class="def-term">A third, if it exists</div>
        <div class="def-body">The live state of one engagement, between the Engagement and the lake. Still an open question, so it is not drawn.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="sidebar-section">
      <div class="sidebar-title">Open questions</div>
      <div id="open-body"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

<footer>
  <div class="footer-text">The Sparq Method · SparqOS relationship map · v0.2</div>
  <div class="footer-text" id="edge-count"></div>
</footer>

<script is:inline>
/* ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   CATEGORIES
   ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
var CATS = {
  engagement: { label: 'The engagement',      color: '#E5E5E5' },
  found:      { label: 'Capability & talent', color: '#F4B84A' },
  delivery:   { label: 'Delivery',            color: '#B0AAEE' },
  store:      { label: 'Store & flow',        color: '#7BB2D4' },
  surface:    { label: 'Client surface',      color: '#35B98F' },
  gtm:        { label: 'GTM & commercial',    color: '#E87070' },
  external:   { label: 'Outside SparqOS',     color: '#9A9A9A' }
};

/* ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   NODES  (x/y = position on the 990x900 canvas)

   depth is a confidence claim, not a UI flag:
     'defined' — there is real internal structure, written down
                 somewhere in this repo, and `interior` reproduces it.
     'none'    — nothing defined inside yet. `needs` says what is
                 missing. Never fabricate an interior to fill this.
   ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
var NODES = [
  {
    id: 'cap', name: 'Capability model', sub: 'what we can do, evidenced',
    cat: 'found', x: 30, y: 250,
    desc: 'What Sparq can do, at what level, and how that is evidenced. It sits upstream of nearly everything: it informs who we hire and place, how the work is run, what we sell, and what we charge. Two of those relationships run back the other way — ADLC and Solutions are where the model gets corrected by contact with reality.',
    depth: 'defined',
    interior: {
      summary: 'Domains hold capabilities; capabilities carry levels. Two level systems are defined — how hard a capability runs for the work at hand, and how it operates with AI.',
      groups: [
        {
          label: 'Domains → capabilities',
          items: [
            'Framing — risk framing, problem framing, direction qualification, pattern recall.',
            'Proving — thin-slice engineering, signal definition & instrumentation, proof slicing.',
            'Deciding — confidence evaluation, confidence-based estimation.',
            'Building — always-runnable delivery, durable architecture.',
            'Evidence — continuous risk surfacing, confidence tracking.',
            'Continuity — context & decision capture, handoff continuity, capability transfer.'
          ],
          source: { label: '/SparqStory/', href: '/SparqStory/' }
        },
        {
          label: 'Intensity levels',
          items: [
            'Five intensities: defining strategy, designing user experience, experimenting with spikes, engineering for production, generating active evidence.',
            'They shift with the type of work — unknown territory, problem discovery, solution shaping, validation, production build, optimization.',
            'Nothing ever reaches zero. The mix changes, not the roster.'
          ],
          source: { label: '/model/operating-model/', href: '/model/operating-model/' }
        },
        {
          label: 'AI maturity levels',
          items: [
            'Assisted → integrated → AI-native.',
            'Maturity is held per capability, not per project — mixed maturity inside one engagement is normal.'
          ],
          source: { label: '/sparqos/', href: '/sparqos/' }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    id: 'talent', name: 'Talent & resourcing', sub: 'who does the work',
    cat: 'found', x: 30, y: 430,
    desc: 'Who we put on the work, and how we source and place them. Downstream of the capability model, in a loop with both ADLC (delivery shows what the staffing actually needs to be) and commercials (what we can staff sets what we can price, and what we price sets what we can staff).',
    depth: 'none',
    needs: 'The bench, the roles, and how a capability level maps to a person exist in practice but are not written down anywhere this map can point to. Until they are, drilling in here would be invention.'
  },
  {
    id: 'shop', name: 'The Shop', sub: 'definition open',
    cat: 'delivery', x: 280, y: 60, open: true,
    desc: 'Currently reads as a build space that feeds GTM IQs & accelerators. Drawn in a loop with ADLC on the assumption that it is a playground where new ways of working get found — if it turns out to be an output channel only, that back-edge comes off the map.',
    note: 'Still unresolved: what The Shop is, and what it turns into.',
    depth: 'none',
    needs: 'No interior, because the node itself is still open. What it is has to be settled before what is inside it can be.'
  },
  {
    id: 'adlc', name: 'ADLC', sub: 'how the work moves',
    cat: 'delivery', x: 280, y: 260,
    desc: 'The engine. ADLC generates the evidence that lands in the data lake, drives the client experience surface, and produces the raw material for GTM IQs & accelerators. Almost every relationship it has runs both ways — the capability model, Solutions, commercials, talent, The Shop and institutional intelligence all shape delivery and get reshaped by it. The engagement is what moves through it.',
    depth: 'defined',
    interior: {
      summary: 'Three types of work, not three phases. They are not sequential and none of them belongs to a single role — all three can be live at once across different capabilities in the same engagement.',
      groups: [
        {
          label: 'Types of work',
          items: [
            'Evidence — build to validate. Active uncertainty reduction through measurable signal.',
            'Commitment — build to operate. Deepening investment where confidence has been earned.',
            'Production learning — signal generation from whatever is already live, software or not.'
          ],
          source: { label: '/sparqos/', href: '/sparqos/' }
        },
        {
          label: 'Loops inside the modes',
          items: [
            'Evidence loop: explore → prototype → validate.',
            'Delivery loop: build → test → deploy → observe.',
            'Both may run at once. The SDLC lives inside the loops; it is not the loops.'
          ],
          source: { label: '/sparqos/', href: '/sparqos/' }
        },
        {
          label: 'What governs movement',
          items: [
            'The governing question: what must be proven — technically, behaviorally, or operationally — before we can responsibly commit further?',
            'Confidence gate: promote, iterate, or pivot.',
            'Evidence backlog → validated solution → delivery backlog → production feature.',
            'Capabilities promote independently. The engagement does not move as a block.'
          ],
          source: { label: '/reference/', href: '/reference/' }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
